  "body": "**Stacked on #476** (#339 slice 1, fixture mesh). Slice 4 of #339 per the triage on the issue: fixture UX.\n\n## What changed\n1. **Browser.**\n   - A model row's context menu (under Models or a setup's Fixtures) offers **Use as fixture (<active setup>)** and **Stop using as fixture**. They reuse the existing `TagFixture` / `UntagFixture` commands, so undo and redo work.\n   - A setup's Fixtures node offers **Import fixture…**, which reuses the existing dialog and activates that setup.\n2. **Mesh state per fixture.**\n   - Each Fixtures row ends in `mesh`, or `box only: <reason>`: open mesh, non-finite, collapsed, over the facet cap, no facets, or shared box. The reasons come from #476's `FixtureMesh::build`.\n   - A mesh refusal is reported ahead of a shared box, since the user can fix it.\n   - The Fixtures page shows the full sentence as a `Collision:` label.\n   - The app helper is `fixture_view::mesh_states`, cached per document version.\n3. **Highlight.** `FixtureHit` names the op, move and band, but not the fixture.\n   - For the selected op, `fixture_struck::struck_by` re-runs the gate's own law against each fixture alone and keeps the ones that reproduce a warned move.\n   - Those fixtures are tinted in the gouge colour, and the op banner names them (\"Strikes fixture: …\").\n   - A warned move no fixture reproduces (e.g. a jaw moved without regenerating) says \"Fixture not resolved for move N … regenerate to re-check\" and tints nothing, rather than guessing.\n   - Display only, cached per document version, op and path.\n\n**Behaviour changes to note:**\n- **Import as fixture is now one undo unit.** The new `ImportFixture` command applies and inverts the import, or the update of an existing name, together with the fixture marker. `crates/ui/tests/fixtures.rs::import_as_fixture_lands_as_two_undo_units` became `…_one_undo_unit`; the test count is unchanged.\n- **A refused import now clears the pending fixture binding**, so it can't tag the next, unrelated import.\n- **`posting::fixture_problems`'s per-op workholding check now calls `fixture_struck::op_hits`**, the same function the highlight uses, so the gate and the viewport can't disagree. Same logic, and app suites green.\n\n`docs/decisions/339-fixture-ux.md`\n\n## How tested\n- App `fixture_ux` (8 tests):\n  - closed, open and NaN mesh states, the shared box, and the version cache;\n  - mark and unmark with undo;\n  - `ImportFixture` fresh and as an update, with undo, redo and refusals;\n  - the struck jaw is named and the clear one isn't;\n  - a moved jaw is reported unresolved, not guessed;\n  - no warnings resolves to nothing.\n- UI `egui_app::fixture_ux_tests` (6 tests):\n  - the menu rows and their commands, through the queue and undo;\n  - the row suffixes;\n  - the tint flag (exactly one part carries `STRUCK_CLASS`) and the banner line;\n  - the unresolved banner;\n  - the Fixtures page's refusal text.\n- **No snapshot PNG touched.**\n- App suites green. In ui, only the three headless-GPU tests fail (no adapter on this Mac), as on main. `clippy -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --tests -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Not exercised (draft until the contributor's GUI check)\nA hands-on check. A test kit is prepared: a project with a struck jaw, a clear jaw, an open-mesh jaw, and a plain model to mark.\n\nChangelog: Fixtures: mark or import a fixture from the browser, see whether each fixture is judged by its mesh or only its box (and why), and see which fixture a warned move strikes (#339)\n\nRefs #339\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
